<title>CANADA: Canada grain body leaves 1997/98 fees unchanged.</title>
<headline>Canada grain body leaves 1997/98 fees unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Canadian Grain Commission on Friday said it will leave its mandatory fees unchanged for the sixth year in a row in the 1997/98 (Aug/July) crop year.</p>
<p>The C$40 million raised in 1996/97 by mandatory CGC inspection, grading, weighing and licensing service fees covered 80 percent of the agency's operating costs.</p>
<p>The balance was offset by optional service fees or by Canada's federal government.</p>
<p>&quot;Because there are limits to what can be achieved through streamlining, we may have to adjust some of our optional service fees,&quot; CGC chief commissioner Barry Senft said.</p>
<p>No decisions have yet been made on optional service fees, the CGC statement said.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
